{
  "$comment": [
    "Shared note-content fixtures, exercised by both language implementations.",
    "ADR-0007 requires the TypeScript renderer and the Rust renderer to agree on",
    "the same GFM subset, and this file is the artefact that keeps them honest:",
    "TypeScript reads it in the editor tests, Rust reads it in the validator",
    "tests, and the Rust renderer will read it when export lands.",
    "",
    "`valid` entries must pass validation in both languages. `text` is the plain",
    "text a renderer must produce for the entry, which is what lets a future",
    "renderer be checked against the same rows without encoding a DOM shape here.",
    "",
    "`invalid` entries must be refused in both languages, for the stated reason.",
    "",
    "`markdown_repeat` builds oversized content without putting it in this file:",
    "`unit` repeated `count` times.",
    "",
    "Absolute URLs appear here deliberately and only here. `packages/editor/src`",
    "must contain none, because that directory is bundled into the offline remote",
    "form, whose build guard rejects any absolute URL in the built bytes."
  ],

  "reasons": [
    "empty",
    "too_large",
    "raw_html",
    "link_scheme",
    "control_character"
  ],

  "valid": [
    {
